## Sequence Detector for "1101"

### FSM (Finite State Machine)

The sequence detector can be designed using a Mealy machine.

States: S0, S1, S2, S3, S4

*   S0: Initial state
*   S1: Received "1"
*   S2: Received "11"
*   S3: Received "110"
*   S4: Received "1101"

Transition Table:

| Current State | Input | Next State | Output |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| S0 | 1 | S1 | 0 |
| S0 | 0 | S0 | 0 |
| S1 | 1 | S2 | 0 |
| S1 | 0 | S0 | 0 |
| S2 | 1 | S3 | 0 |
| S2 | 0 | S0 | 0 |
| S3 | 1 | S4 | 0 |
| S3 | 0 | S0 | 0 |
| S4 | 1 | S1 | 1 |
| S4 | 0 | S0 | 0 |

### VHDL Implementation

```vhdl
library ieee;
use ieee.std_logic_1164.all;

entity sequence_detector is
    Port ( clk : in STD_LOGIC;
           reset : in STD_LOGIC;
           input : in STD_LOGIC;
           output : out STD_LOGIC);
end sequence_detector;

architecture Behavioral of sequence_detector is
type state_type is (S0, S1, S2, S3, S4);
signal state, next_state : state_type;
begin
    process(clk, reset)
    begin
        if reset = '1' then
            state <= S0;
        elsif rising_edge(clk) then
            state <= next_state;
        end if;
    end process;

    process(state, input)
    begin
        case state is
            when S0 =>
                if input = '1' then
                    next_state <= S1;
                else
                    next_state <= S0;
                end if;
                output <= '0';
            when S1 =>
                if input = '1' then
